---
const principles = [
  { title: 'One point person', text: 'We work closely with one person on your team, so the know-how stays in your building.' },
  { title: 'We teach as we go', text: 'By the end, your point person can train the next new hire without us.' },
  { title: "It's all yours", text: 'Every plan, checklist and document we make, you keep and can change.' },
  { title: 'Nothing to sell you', text: 'No vendor pays us for recommending their product.' },
  { title: "We'll come to you", text: "Most of it happens over video. When it needs to be in person, we'll drive. Colebrook included." },
  { title: 'We call back', text: "You'll hear from us within three business days." },
];
---
<section id="approach" class="container section-pad" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
  <div class="layout">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
      <h2 id="approach-title" class="h2">Built for places where the office manager is also the IT department.</h2>
      <p class="lede">That's most practices we know. So we keep it simple, and we plan for the day we're not around anymore.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="grid">
      {principles.map((p) => (
        <li>
          <h3 class="item-title">{p.title}</h3>
          <p class="item-text">{p.text}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .layout {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 48px;
  }

  .intro {
    flex: 1 1 340px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .h2 { margin-bottom: 20px; }

  .grid {
    flex: 1.4 1 420px;
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(220px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 32px 28px;
  }
</style>
